# {{name}}/.env.example --- copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in.
#
# A LIBRARY declares the keys it needs here and reads them from the process
# environment at use time -- it does NOT load .env itself. Loading the environment on
# a consumer's behalf, at a moment the consumer did not choose, is the ordering bug
# this convention exists to avoid; that call belongs to the application's entry point.
#
# The host environment wins in prod (set real vars there, ship no .env). Add KEY=VALUE
# lines as the project needs them, and `cons` will aggregate them for any app that
# depends on this.

# EXAMPLE_API_KEY=REPLACE_ME
